{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 40, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the sunlight too bright, the birdsong too…perfect. He sat up in bed, a strange awareness prickling at the back of his mind. The floral wallpaper, the antique dresser, the way the dust motes danced in the light – it was all *too* detailed, too crisp. He reached out to steady himself and his hand passed right through the wooden headboard. Panic flared. He looked down at his hands, noticing they were unnaturally smooth, the skin flawless. A notification box, shimmering in his vision, popped up: \"Welcome to Evergreena! Level 1 achieved. Quest: Retrieve the Sunstone from the Goblin Caves.\" He felt a surge of disbelief, then a cold dread. This wasn't his bedroom. This wasn’t real. He was *in* a video game.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled out of bed, his legs shaky, and found himself in a quaint village square. Villagers, with impossibly rosy cheeks and wide, vacant smiles, bustled about their daily routines. A blacksmith hammered glowing metal, a baker pulled loaves of bread from a brick oven, and children chased pigeons with unnerving enthusiasm. The world was vibrant, almost overwhelmingly so. He tried to speak, to ask someone what was happening, but the words caught in his throat. A quest marker appeared above a nearby thatched roof, pulsing with a soft, inviting light. The Sunstone. Goblin Caves. It all felt absurd, yet undeniably real. Arthur took a deep breath, the air smelling of pine and something vaguely metallic, and resigned himself to his new reality. He had a quest.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.18361379206180573}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.32705190777778625}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0002044230350293219}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.10078337788581848}, {"token": "▁sunlight", "logprob": -1.43425714969635}, {"token": "▁too", "logprob": -2.0663211345672607}, {"token": "▁bright", "logprob": -0.42974